240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 176 0 R
/T (training and validation setup)
/E (training and validation setup)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (The training and validation data configuration in this project adopts a Hold-Out Validation approach, splitting the balanced 3,300-row financial dataset into a proportion of 80% for training data and 20% for testing data. The data splitting process is strictly implemented using the stratified splitting method to ensure that the distribution of the three sentiment classes \(each consisting of 1,100 rows for the Positive, Neutral, and Negative classes\) remains proportionally preserved across both the training and testing subsets.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Furthermore, during the experimentation and SVM model tuning phase, the team implemented a 5-Fold Cross-Validation mechanism directly integrated with GridSearchCV, optimized against the weighted F1-score metric. This combination of stratified data partitioning and five-fold cross-validation is systematically designed to reinforce evaluation reliability, mitigate the risk of overfitting, and ensure the model can objectively generalize sentiments from new economic news movements.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
