332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Link
/P 519 0 R
/Alt (The problem formulation in this project is rooted in the high volume of dailydigital financial news reporting, which makes it difficult for stakeholders tomanually monitor shifts in public perception regarding economic policies. Thismanual monitoring has proven to have strategic weaknesses, as it is highlyvulnerable to human bias and frequently obscures positive achievements dueto elevated regulatory noise stemming from massive news frequencies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [225 0 R 637 0 R 638 0 R 639 0 R 640 0 R 641 0 R 642 0 R]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Link
/P 520 0 R
/Alt (To address these challenges, this problem is formulated into a natural languageprocessing \(NLP\) machine learning task: automated sentiment classificationusing the Support Vector Machine \(SVM\) algorithm. Through an end-to-endsystem integrated into a real-time web application, this model is designed tocut through information clutter by delivering objective, consistent, and data-driven sentiment analysis of Indonesian financial news.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [226 0 R 643 0 R 644 0 R 645 0 R 646 0 R 647 0 R 648 0 R]
>>
endobj
