519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The problem formulation in this project is rooted in the high volume of daily digital financial news reporting, which makes it difficult for stakeholders to manually monitor shifts in public perception regarding economic policies. This manual monitoring has proven to have strategic weaknesses, as it is highly vulnerable to human bias and frequently obscures positive achievements due to elevated regulatory noise stemming from massive news frequencies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [332 0 R]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (To address these challenges, this problem is formulated into a natural language processing \(NLP\) machine learning task: automated sentiment classification using the Support Vector Machine \(SVM\) algorithm. Through an end-to-end system integrated into a real-time web application, this model is designed to cut through information clutter by delivering objective, consistent, and data-driven sentiment analysis of Indonesian financial news.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [333 0 R]
>>
endobj
